     user-visible inconsistency exists.
   FINDING (backlog, OUT OF SCOPE for CB5): bucketMajorExpenses and
   handleMajorExpenseDrilldown sum a shared transaction list in different
   orders, producing float64 noise on the order of 1e-15 between a
   group's/Unmatched's list-row total and its own drilldown total. Never
   observed to cross a display-rounding boundary in probing, but the two
   summation orders are not pinned to agree, which is the kind of thing
   ruling 2026-08-29b/W2 flags as a latent dual-formatter risk. This
   predates CB5 (reproduced identically on CB4's matched-group credits
   path) and is not something this task's diff touched or could have
   fixed within its written scope — recommend a follow-up task to make
   both call sites sum in the same order (e.g. always in ts-provided
   order, or both post the same sort) rather than relying on floating
   point tolerance.

